---@class posthog.messaging.MessagingSendEmailCreateRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field to string Email address of the recipient.
---@field message_data? posthog.messaging.MessagingSendEmailCreateRequestMessageDataMap Data for the template's Liquid placeholders, available as `variables`. For example `{"reset_link": "https://..."}` fills `{{ variables.reset_link }}`.
---@field template_id? string ID of the email template to send. The template must be made transactional first. Send either `template_id` or `template_key`.
---@field template_key? string Names an email whose content your code rendered, such as `order-shipped`, so its metrics, logs and status group under it. Letters, numbers, hyphens (-) and underscores (_) only. Send it with `subject` and `html` or `text`. PostHog sends the content as is and never stores it as a template.
---@field distinct_id? string|distilled.Null Distinct ID of the recipient's person. The email's engagement events (sent, delivered, opened, clicked, bounced) and the send itself are recorded against that person. Defaults to the recipient's email address. The template can't read the person's properties, so pass everything it needs in `message_data`.
---@field subject? string Subject of the email your code rendered.
---@field html? string HTML body of the email your code rendered, at most 5 MiB as UTF-8.
---@field text? string Plain text body of the email your code rendered, at most 5 MiB as UTF-8. Without it, PostHog derives the text from `html`.
---@field reply_to? posthog.messaging.MessagingSendEmailCreateRequestReplyToList Addresses replies to the email your code rendered go to.
---@field cc? posthog.messaging.MessagingSendEmailCreateRequestCc|distilled.Null Addresses that get a visible copy of the email your code rendered: one address, or a list of up to 10. Each is a bare address such as `jane@example.com`, with no name. Doesn't apply to a send with `template_id`, which refuses any address here.
---@field bcc? posthog.messaging.MessagingSendEmailCreateRequestBcc|distilled.Null Addresses that get a hidden copy of the email your code rendered: one address, or a list of up to 10. Each is a bare address such as `jane@example.com`, with no name. Doesn't apply to a send with `template_id`, which refuses any address here.
---@field attachments? posthog.messaging.MessagingSendEmailCreateRequestAttachmentsList|distilled.Null Files attached to the email your code rendered: up to 10, and at most 512 KB in total after decoding. File types mailbox providers block, such as `.exe`, are refused. Doesn't apply to a send with `template_id`, which refuses any file here.
---@field capture_engagement? boolean Whether the engagement events (sent, delivered, opened, clicked, bounced) of the email your code rendered are captured as analytics events of the recipient. Defaults to true. A project whose admin turned engagement capture off captures nothing, whatever the send says.
---@field from? string Sender of the email your code rendered, as `security@example.com` or `Example <security@example.com>`, on a verified domain of the project. Without it, the email goes out from the project's default sender, or from its only verified sender when it has no default.

